"You can provide either a fake backend or a hardware backend from Qiskit "
"Runtime.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpile the circuit, visualize the swaps, and note the depth {#transpile-"
"the-circuit-visualize-the-swaps-and-note-the-depth}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We choose a layout that requires two swaps to execute the gates between "
"qubits 3 and 0 and another two swaps to return the qubits to their initial "
"positions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/cutting/02-gate-cutting-to-"
"reduce-circuit-depth/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Replace distant gates with `TwoQubitQPDGate`s by specifying their indices "
"{#replace-distant-gates-with-twoqubitqpdgates-by-specifying-their-indices}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`cut_gates` will replace the gates in the specified indices with "
"`TwoQubitQPDGate`s and also return a list of `QPDBasis` instances -- one for"
" each gate decomposition.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/cutting/02-gate-cutting-to-"
"reduce-circuit-depth/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate the subexperiments to run on the backend {#generate-the-"
"subexperiments-to-run-on-the-backend}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`generate_cutting_experiments` accepts a circuit containing "
"`TwoQubitQPDGate` instances and observables as a `PauliList`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate the expectation value of the full-sized circuit, many "
"subexperiments are generated from the decomposed gates' joint "
"quasiprobability distribution and then executed on one or more backends. The"
" number of samples taken from the distribution is controlled by "
"`num_samples`, and one combined coefficient is given for each unique sample."
" For more information on how the coefficients are calculated, refer to the "
"[explanatory material](../explanation/index.rst).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** The ``observables`` kwarg to `generate_cutting_experiments` is of "
"type `PauliList`. Observable term coefficients and phases are ignored during"
" decomposition of the problem and execution of the subexperiments. They may "
"be re-applied during reconstruction of the expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the sampling overhead for the chosen cuts {#calculate-the-"
"sampling-overhead-for-the-chosen-cuts}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we cut three CNOT gates, resulting in a sampling overhead of $9^3$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more on the sampling overhead incurred by circuit cutting, refer to the "
"[explanatory material](../explanation/index.rst).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Demonstrate that the QPD subexperiments will be shallower after cutting "
"distant gates {#demonstrate-that-the-qpd-subexperiments-will-be-shallower-"
"after-cutting-distant-gates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is an example of an arbitrarily chosen subexperiment generated from the"
" QPD circuit. Its depth has been reduced by more than half. Many of these "
"probabilistic subexperiments must be generated and evaluated in order to "
"reconstruct an expectation value of the deeper circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

